        "J2.3",
        "U2.2",
        "U3.2"
      ],
      "nets": [
        "TACH",
        "GND",
        "VCC"
      ],
      "observed": "The TACH net is pulled up to VCC through R6 10k and also connected to a component D1 valued 1K to GND; D1 is drawn/valued as a 1 kΩ resistor despite the diode reference.",
      "expected": "A fan tachometer input normally uses only a pull-up or a correctly specified clamp diode; a 1 kΩ resistor to GND would be a strong pulldown, and a diode reference should not carry a resistance value.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "TACH ... D1 1K ... GND and R6 10K TACH VCC (sheet /, top/right area)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "Atmel/ ... an ATtiny-driven fan controller"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If D1 is assembled as a 1 kΩ resistor, the TACH input is pulled low by the R6/D1 divider and fan RPM feedback is likely lost; if a diode was intended, the value/reference is wrong.",
      "confidence": 0.62
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic shows at least two likely deviations: the ATtiny13V-10S footprint U3 has its PB0/PB1/PB2 pins shifted relative to the actual part pinout, and the TACH input contains a D1/1K component that behaves as a strong pulldown or is misidentified as a resistor/diode."
}

